14)Explain the architecture of Kubernetes — API Server, Controller Manager, Scheduler, etc.
1)Control Plane Componenets(Master Node)
API Server: “Kubernetes receptionist + gatekeeper” ,Front-door of Kubernetes; exposes REST APIs, validates requests, and updates etcd
etcd: “Kubernetes database”, Distributed key-value store that stores the cluster state (source of truth of Kubernetes)
Controller Manager: “Maintains desired state — keeps things running as defined” , Ensures desired state; runs controllers like Node, Deployment, ReplicaSet controllers
Scheduler: “Decides where a pod should run”, Assigns pods to worker nodes based on resource usage, constraints, taints/tolerations
2)Worker Node Components
Kubelet: Agent on each node that receives pod specs and ensures containers run as expected.
Container Runtime: Runs the containers (e.g., Docker, containerd, CRI-O).
Kube-Proxy: Maintains cluster networking and service communication (load balances traffic).

15)How Components Work Together (High-Level Flow)?
User sends a request (kubectl apply) → API Server
API Server stores the desired state → etcd
Controller Manager notices difference between desired and current state
Scheduler picks a node for the Pod
Kubelet on that node runs the pod using the container runtime
Kube-Proxy routes network traffic to/from the pod

