31)Explain the difference between readiness and liveness probes.
Readiness Probe checks if the application is ready to serve traffic. If it fails, the pod is removed from the service load balancer.
Liveness Probe checks if the application is healthy. If it fails, Kubernetes restarts the container.
| Feature        | Readiness Probe                    | Liveness Probe                       |
| Checks         | If app is ready to serve traffic   | If app is alive or stuck             |
| Failure Action | Pod removed from Service endpoints | Container is restarted               |
| Traffic Impact | No traffic sent until ready        | Restart can cause temporary downtime |
| When used      | Startup and during runtime         | During runtime health                |

