33)How can you perform zero-downtime deployment in Kubernetes?
1. Rolling Updates (Default Deployment Strategy) : Kubernetes gradually replaces old pods with new ones — keeping the app running.
2. Readiness Probes (Very Important) : Only send traffic to a pod after it's ready.
3. Liveness Probes : Ensures faulty pods are auto-restarted and kept healthy.
4. PodDisruptionBudget (PDB) : Prevents too many pods from being down at the same time.
5. Stop Sending Traffic to Old Pods Before Killing Them : Use terminationGracePeriodSeconds and preStop hook to drain connections.
6. Use Multi-Version Support (Optional, for Canary/Blue-Green)
| Strategy       | Best For                  | Downtime |
| Rolling Update | Standard apps             | None     |
| Blue-Green     | High-risk releases        | None     |
| Canary         | Testing with % of traffic | None     |

