42)Explain what happens when you run kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml.
kubectl apply → API Server → etcd → Deployment Controller → ReplicaSet → Scheduler → Kubelet → Container Runtime → Pod Running
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml sends the manifest to the API server, which validates and stores it in etcd as the desired state. 
The Deployment controller notices the new or updated state and creates or updates a ReplicaSet. 
The ReplicaSet ensures the correct number of Pods exist. 
The Scheduler assigns those Pods to nodes, and the kubelet on each node pulls the container image and starts the containers. Probes, networking, and service endpoints are then configured.”

